    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37537" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-dŏcĕo</span></b> ,
			cŭi, ctum, 2, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to teach</i>, <i>instruct</i>, <i>inform
			beforehand</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illi praedocti a duce arma mutaverant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. J. 94, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedoctus esto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 34, 77, § 334</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">myrrheus Pulvis sepulcrum praedocet,</span>”
				<i>points out</i>, <i>shows</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Cath. 12, 72</span></i>
			.</div>
